  "title": "How often?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Frequency words usually come early in the sentence, before the object and verb: **আমি প্রতিদিন অফিসে যাই** 'I go to the office every day'.\n\n- **প্রতিদিন** — every day\n- **সবসময়** — always\n- **মাঝে মাঝে** — sometimes\n- **কখনো … না** — never\n\nFor 'never', put **কখনো** before the verb and **না** after it: **আমি কখনো মাছ খাই না** 'I never eat fish'. As a one-word reply, **কখনো না!** 'Never!'\n\n**Culture:** Muslims say **নামাজ পড়া** — literally 'read the prayer'. The call to prayer five times a day is one of the most familiar sounds of Bangladesh.",
